Process

	1. Git
		1.1 It is essential for anyone in IT to know about git basics since that is how we reach for other people's projects and coordinate with other people if we are included in one. And even if we want to keep track of our own project's change history.
		1.2 Trainer has a commandable hands-on mindset and wants to teach everything and also this bit with practice. So he develops and simple app and we go through the git workflow with this application.
		1.3 Git workflow
			I. Change to the root/main directory of the project
			II. Now we need to enable git in this folder by telling it.
				-'git initialize' is used for this purpose
			III. Now we need to put the code on stage first, so we can watch it. It's like putting your play on stage, like a theatre
				-'git add .' is used
			IV. Finally we contribute/commit our code to the project's code
				-"git commit -m 'This is our app'" is used 
