	2. Git remote repositories
		2.1 When working collaborately we need a main repository to place and retrieve the code.
			I. We can install git on on-premise server or use gitlab/github on cloud
		2.2 we can tell our local git that there is a remote repository
			I. git remote add <github> <http/ssh_link>
				- We will be using this name we ourselves have give to push our local code.
		2.3 To push our code to the remote repository
			I. git push github main
		2.4 To clonde/download a remote repository/project
			I. git clone <link>
		2.5 To get the recent changes from a repo
			I. git pull 
